     interrupts or races the admitted one. ``False`` when no authority serves the scope or the
     route holds no committed human turn to borrow provenance from: the caller keeps the adapter
-    path (nothing is queued there either). Raises ``RuntimeStoreError`` on a refusal."""
+    path (nothing is queued there either). Raises ``RuntimeStoreError`` on a refusal.
+
+    A goal wake (a Kanban wake bound to ``expected_goal_id``, or a ``goal-continuation``) also
+    yields ``False`` while the runner drains (``_draining`` restart/shutdown, or the reversible
+    ``_external_drain_active`` marker drain): the authority's admission gate only checks
+    ``_draining``, so without this yield an active goal's wake->turn->wake loop keeps admissions
+    started and a drain never reaches idle. ``False`` is the paused-goal deferral, not a discard:
+    the Kanban notifier leaves the event unseen for a later tick or the next owner, and the
+    continuation hook admits no next turn, so the in-flight work drains to zero."""
+    if expected_goal_id is not None or producer == 'goal-continuation':
+        from gateway.platforms.api_server_fire_startup import runner_is_draining
+        if runner_is_draining(runner):
+            return False
